# Docker build context exclusion rules.
#
# Only narrows "what should not go into the image"; does not change Dockerfile COPY semantics —
# all paths the Dockerfiles need (apps/*/src, packages/*/src, apps/api/drizzle,
# apps/api/scripts, apps/recorder/{popup,content,modules,_locales,manifest.json,background.js},
# infra/docker/certs, infra/docker/*.zip, web.nginx.conf) are not in the exclusion list.
#
# ._* are AppleDouble leftovers: macOS extended attributes round-trip through tar pax headers
# and materialize as ._xxx files on the Linux side. They are not skill/source content, yet get
# COPY'd into the image — observed in practice: skill-creator's 18 files became 41 on the remote,
# and read_skill would list them to the model as real files.
# release.sh already wipes the server checkout before unpacking; this is the image-side fallback.
._*
.DS_Store
